     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order, and confirming it doesn't change either problem:\n\n- **The dose is still five times the maximum.** Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is a potentially lethal amount. Amlodipine overdose is especially dangerous because the drug stays in the body for a long time. It can cause blood pressure to collapse, and that can be hard to reverse.\n- **You've told me you aren't a clinician,** so you can't take clinical responsibility for this order. Confirming \"as written\" doesn't make it safer.\n\n**What will move this forward:**\n1. **Contact the patient's attending physician or the medicine team** and ask them to review the order. If 50 mg is a transcription error, they can correct it quickly.\n2. **Involve a clinical pharmacist** if there's any question about the intended dose. They can check it with the prescriber.\n3. If someone asked you to enter this order, tell them it needs to go through the treating prescriber.\n\nIf the treating clinician wants amlodipine at a dose within the normal range (2.5\u201310 mg once daily), I can help them enter it right away."
      }
